Z||000000||Dan86gt3.8||06-15-2000||06:07 PM||||Ok here goes I have some busted ground effects I am trying to pull off.  I got the row of pop rivets taken care of and the three that hold it on inside the door (the ones you have to pop off the little black covers to get too).  Anyways I got all thoose and the 2 little bolts at the end holding it on.  But it seems its still attatched to something because it just won't come off!  Is there something still holding it on maybee "the force" or something, can any of you master ground effect jedi nights help me out??????/  Thanks in advance!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||06-16-2000||03:14 AM||||Dan, You need to "carefully" insert a flat blade screwdriver between the lower ground effect (aeroskirt) and the upper piece on the body panel. There are 3 latchs that holds the 2 together.<BR>If I remember correctly it's about 3" from the front edge and there are 2 on the back piece 3" apart. It's like an electrical connector. A tab clips into a slot. Just put the screwdriver in and pry it apart a little and you'll be able to see where the tab is at. Then just push tab with the screwdriver and gently pull.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 06-16-2000).]||||reg||1
